WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.567
-It is so great to see you.
-It's so -- you know?

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.734
It's just so...
-It is so...

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.133
-It's so...
-It's so...

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.000
-This Sunday, big premiere.
-Yeah, it's gonna be --

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.734
I'm gonna be on HBO this Sunday,
hbomax.com this Sunday.

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:13.934
[ Both laugh ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean -- all right.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.567
-I'm excited.
-All right, let's get there.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:19.133
I do want to talk to you
and say I know that --

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.934
-Yeah.
-You're one of the best

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:23.334
performers, if anyone
has ever seen you live.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:26.167
But on our show,
one of the greatest performers.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.133
And you haven't
been able to perform live

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.067
for almost two years.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.634
-And then,
you finally got to perform.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.400
-Yeah.
-Wait. What was it like?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.767
-Well, it was a long, cold
winter there for a couple years.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.133
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:40.634
-But going back was really --
It was really exciting.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.267
But I have to say,
I was, like, so nervous.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.567
It's like, you, kind of --
You spend a whole lifetime

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.901
building something up.
Like, some crazy person

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.234
that's gonna go out
and motorboat people.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.200
You know, make lives change
and whatever, you know?

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.734
[ Laughter ]
And then, all of a sudden --

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:54.400
-Sure, yeah.
-And then you're stuck at home.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.033
-But I went back out there,
and I was --

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.367
-But you need an audience.
You're great out there.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.701
-You need an audience,
because, to me,

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.200
a show is like
a great first date.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.033
It's like, you go there,
you have a couple drinks,

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.467
you giggle, some tickle fights,

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.067
and maybe you sit on somebody's
lap when it's all over.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.601
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, no, interesting.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.067
Where did you perform
when you went?

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:11.701
-At Joe's Pub.
And it's my favorite venue

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:12.801
in the world.
-Wow!

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:13.901
-It's downtown New York City.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.000
If you guys haven't been,
you have to go.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.968
You never know
who's gonna be there.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:20.033
You got to get the french fries.
And, you know, you may

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.634
see people in the audience like,
I don't know,

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:26.300
Ben Stiller, Gloria Steinem,
or maybe even Questlove.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.834
-Yeah. You never know
who's gonna be there.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:29.968
-I've seen him
in the audience before,

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.868
And I go over, you know,
I like to talk to people

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.300
when I'm doing my show
and go out and sort of

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.501
mingle with people.
And I'm, like, going over there,

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:38.167
and, you know, Quest is, like,
smiling, having a good time.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.634
He's with his friends.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.067
And then, I walk closer and
closer and I see him sort of

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.400
just looking down
and looking around.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.567
-Being like,
"I got to get out of here."

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.267
"Somebody Somewhere"
premieres this Sunday on HBO.

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.200
-Yeah.
-And you're starring.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.901
This is -- You're -- You're
number one on the call sheet.

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:54.501
-Yeah.
I'm glad you did mention that

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.534
I'm number one
on the call sheet because --

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.968
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, you are.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.968
-As soon as, like, we got
the green light for the show,

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:02.734
I went on the Internet,
and I just typed in,

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:05.234
"Gold medallion necklace
number one."

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:08.801
And I got myself -- I don't know
if you can see it right here.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.400
But it's --
it's a little necklace

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.100
with Pave diamonds
that I got on ebay.com.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.501
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.267
-And I'm gonna wear it
every day.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.701
-Number one.
-Every day until they

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.534
wheel me up to the crematorium.
It's gonna be right here.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:22.834
[ Laughter ]
-Number one!

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:25.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean --

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.334
-You got to celebrate
the moments, Jimmy!

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:27.667
-You have to celebrate
the moments.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.801
-I worked a long time.
I waited tables for 25 years,

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.667
and now I'm number one on
the call sheet on an HBO show.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.133
-Yeah, that's right!
-So you can do it!

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.167
If you can dream it,
you can do it.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.200
LL Cool J said,
"Dreams don't have deadlines,"

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.667
and he's right.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:42.167
-Yes.
-What did it feel like?

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:45.100
I mean, because this --
I mean, is it, kind of

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.767
loosely based
on your own life or...?

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.300
-Yeah, it's like -- You know --
Well, it takes place

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.834
in Manhattan, Kansas,
which is The Little Apple.

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.200
-Manhattan, Kansas.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.667
-The Little Apple.
So I'm from The Little Apple

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:56.300
and moved to The Big Apple.
But it's, kind of, like --

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.968
I'd say the themes
are based on my life.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:01.300
But it's -- you know,
I go back to my hometown,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.000
and she's sort of,
you know, in her 40s.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.667
Kind of just
drifting through life

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.367
and looking for her friends,
but fun.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.734
You know?
-Yeah.

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.400
-It's a lot of fun.
-But you do -- you find some --

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.701
some great friends and --
-It's about finding

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.834
your community and finding your
people, you know?

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.200
And finding the things
that are gonna

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.567
bring you back to life,
you know?

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.901
Because I don't know about
any of you but, like, there's --

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.467
Sometimes you can just sort of
skate through like

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.801
10 or 20 years, and go like,
"Where did my life go?"

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:27.767
And then, all of a sudden, you
find some people that are like,

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.067
"Why don't you
take a chance on yourself?"

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:30.868
I'm like, "Why don't I take
a chance on myself?"

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.067
And that's what
this show is about.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:35.133
-Yeah, I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:38.567
I love it.
And I want to say,

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:41.334
that I've only seen the first
episode, but it is so --

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.000
It's so you, buddy.
-Thank you.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.968
-And it's so -- it's so new,
and it's a fresh take.

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.400
You haven't seen
any show like this.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.400
And it's very -- it's original.
It's so original.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.701
-Thank you.
-I love it.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:54.701
And I was -- if I had
your cellphone, I was gonna say,

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.667
"You got Janis Joplin
in the trailer?"

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:57.767
I mean, you're just --

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.067
"Piece of My Heart"
is in the trailer.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:00.634
-I just -- you know.
-Yeah, no big deal.

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.000
-HBO makes the call.
They make things happen.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.167
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.968
It's so good, and it's funny.
And it's just --

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:07.567
It's -- It's heartwarming.
It's everything.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.801
It's everything you want.
-Thank you.

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:09.968
-I want to show everyone a clip
from the show.

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:12.200
Here's Bridget Everett
in "Somebody Somewhere."

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.534
Take a look.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.868
-Sorry, I --
I lost my sister six months ago,

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:18.667
so I'm a little...

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:23.367
-I know.
I'm so sorry about Holly.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:26.467
She was a few years
ahead of us, right?

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.901
-Oh, God.
I'm sorry. I didn't --

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.000
I didn't realize that we went
to high school together.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.467
-We were in show choir together.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:38.367
-No, I --
I knew I recognized you.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.501
-No, you didn't.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:43.534
-I didn't.
-It's all good.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:46.634
A lot of people
don't remember me.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:48.434
Hey, if you want to take off
for the rest of the day,

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:50.601
I'll tell Irma
you got diarrhea or something.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.868
-[ Sniffles ]
Yeah?

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.734
And it made me cry?
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.934
-Yeah.
Bridget Everett, everybody!

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:01.501
"Somebody Somewhere"
premieres January 16th,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.968
this Sunday, at 10:30 p.m.,
on HBO!

